<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26909" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŏcūtor</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŏquūtor</span></b> ),
			ōris, m.
		loquor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>one who speaks, a speaker</i> (post-class.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rudis locutor exotici sermonis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 1, p. 102</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			partic., <i>a talker, prater, babbler</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">leves et futiles et importuni locutores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					1, 15, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
